# 8c with real git: two tasks side by side, each in a copy of the code of its
# own, and one that waits for both. The second is checked with the first's
# accepted work merged into its folder, and the third is cut from the
# collected work, so its check sees both. Then the work is landed.
agent A.1: edit header.txt | commit | write-result | report done "the header is in"
agent B.1: edit footer.txt | commit | write-result | report done "the footer is in"
agent C.1: edit page.txt | commit | write-result | report done "the page is joined"

file brief.md: Target: a small page | Change: your part of it | Constraints: none | Ownership: your own file | Acceptance: the check passes
git
orch: init
orch: run new "a small page"                        -> expect r1
task A "Write the header" --name header --check "test -f header.txt" --brief brief.md
task B "Write the footer" --name footer --check "test -f footer.txt && test -f header.txt" --brief brief.md
task C "Join the page" --name "whole page" --after header,footer --check "test -f header.txt && test -f footer.txt && test -f page.txt" --brief brief.md
orch: start --ready                                 -> expect "(A.1)" "(B.1)"
await: attempts A.1 reported, B.1 reported
orch: wait --timeout 10                             -> expect done A.1 B.1
orch: accept A                                      -> expect "A is done, checked"
orch: accept footer                                 -> expect "B is done, checked" "Ready now: C"
orch: start --ready                                 -> expect "(C.1)"
await: attempts C.1 reported
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 10                  -> expect done C
orch: accept C                                      -> expect "C is done, checked"
orch: close --settled                               -> expect "the copy of the code of A" "the copy of the code of C" stays
orch: wait --ack last --timeout 0
orch: land --local                                  -> expect exit 5 "Only the person"
human: land --local                                 -> expect "main"
orch: run close

assert: A status done; B status done; C status done; attempts A.1 accepted, B.1 accepted, C.1 accepted
